{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: observability Draft 5 exact 27fbdfd217e60bf4c6907e028d92d056769d8efe, tree 755c4eb9199d372bfaafeaf2a861a01ccce83012. Two narrow consistency repairs remain; the main Draft 4 corrections are answered.\n\nP2 — Give the single summary row consistent per-kind domains and witnesses (§4.2/§4.4/W1).\nThe summary correctly has reason summary, double2 a loss bitmask and double6 groups merged. The global slot definitions still require double2 to be a duration or zero and double6 to be a flag count no greater than multiplicity. One summary event can count multiple merged groups, so it violates that stated domain. Explicitly define the summary's per-kind numeric meanings, limits and saturation, and make the validator accept that row. Old prose still emits reason tainted and sidecar; W1 still expects groups and sidecar rows. Those variants were removed from the closed reason union and conflict with exactly one terminal summary. Each loss must update that one summary's bits/counts; update every witness accordingly. Include mixed reasons and group counts greater than one in one invocation, with one valid summary and the hard write cap respected.\n\nP2 — Cover the native turn exit that bypasses #close (§4.2/§4.7).\nThe design says #close is the one place every turn passes. Native turn.ts:209 returns End.unavailable immediately when its definition is absent, and run:188 returns that step directly. It bypasses #close, so metrics emitted only there miss that turn. Use a common run exit or explicitly instrument every exit, and add a missing-definition/unavailable witness alongside ordinary public and internal turns. Define the route's operational flag for Worker and DO early no-turn answers, from actual execution/observation, without changing public answer bytes. This completes the promised turn-boundary coverage; no full RPC-body audit or new runtime failure is claimed.\n\nArchitecture, Security and Simplification: one reserved summary bitmask, group65 bounded coarsening, mixed fields/IDs, internal boolean answer none, checked saturation and multiplicity formulas materially repair the earlier findings. Sampled windows are now unknown/fail rather than using an invented confidence bound; observed busy fails regardless. Paired loss and unmatched alarm/give-up limitations are explicitly declared and accepted as limits of observed telemetry, not demands for an impossible absence proof. Earlier true-age expiry, admin sidecar isolation, strict trace/privacy separation, readiness/selector, observational timeout, partial read heads and version/error taxonomy remain preserved. Keep the complete functionality; estimates remove no scope.\n\nCoverage: primary FIRST FULL Root 45383B/608LF SHA e41ba89d3f94bf609a3d59543d60e740a92e9da690f67f0c0f841963e8e3714e. U3 FULL peers 24844B/285LF SHA bfc48e06beb945b260ea101dfc968bfc17677c94387f57bf4b7d69b366c7f6da. Both peer finals/audits FULL Root; primary/U3 hashes and 12 architecture/8 security Source identities independently verified with prior FULL/fragments kept distinct. Fresh native turn146–234 units FULL Root and hashes verified. Audit /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-checker-state/observability-D5-root-native-audit.json, 2261B/SHA9d750b1d6264abd1fd3dc16ee222930a49840d6deb5872eda6d8cd2ce2c0ba29. No Source/tests/build/gate/provider/browser/private woo/log execution. W1–W3 and calibration remain future UNRUN. Normal prepare assigned original5a6/626/main only.\n","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03b00598a91160fd89aa9e7ac3ca2d3f28f2c3cb","binding":"assigned","head":"27fbdfd217e60bf4c6907e028d92d056769d8efe","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:468e63df56b63903e2484ca4aad75d518575e55a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6264f1e8e28666333a7c9564e5cb74a347b33a7c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git: